      "translatedText": "Then use the make command to compile, the command is`make`or`make -jxx`, here xx is the number of CPU threads you want to use for compilation\\. For example, my computer has 8 cores and 16 threads, so I can set xx to a number lower than 16\\. And`make`uses one thread by default\\. If you do not know how many threads your CPU has, then just honestly use the`make`command, and do not use the`make -jxx`command\\.",
